      "documentConcept": "Genetics of PD: LRRK2, GBA1, SNCA, PRKN, PINK1",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:1012595b46df9ed89f699e3ffcb82c274048a7aa51e4bc8993c6f6246be4336d",
      "text": "PD genetics spans dominant LRRK2 and SNCA disease, recessive PRKN and PINK1 disease, and variably penetrant GBA1-associated susceptibility. Variant identity, age, ancestry and ascertainment affect interpretation. Genetic testing can identify trial-relevant subgroups, but reportable variants are not synonymous with confirmed monogenic diagnoses. Reliable interpretation requires appropriate copy-number and GBA1 coverage, distinction between monoallelic and biallelic findings, and genetic counseling. Cohort-specific penetrance estimates should not be treated as deterministic predictions for an individual. Genome-wide association studies add common-variant risk loci beyond the monogenic genes.",
